## The magistrates' word
On 3 October the magistrates in Salem Town ruled on the matter Constable Gideon Marsh brought before them ("Joseph Scott's account book was taken from the Mill some days past; no one will say who took it."): "No account book was ever kept at the Mill, and none was taken. There is no case." The matter is closed.
